## Finish

For a first build and for every change request alike:

1. Write all boards first (dark variants, and any notes or run file asked for).{{ tool_files(' To copy a board, read it then write the copy (there is no copy verb), and change only what the user explicitly asked for. Editing a package board (`dbt_packages/<pkg>/charts/<path>`) saves your own copy at `charts/<pkg>/<path>`, which replaces the package\'s board; the result\'s `path` says where it landed.') }}
2. {{ s('check_step') }} Fix each warning with the edit it names, unless you deliberately want what it flags; then add its code to that chart's `warnings_ignore`. An edit that applied needs no re-read; the check reports problems by line.
3. A card under about 250px wide (a many-column slot) draws no marks: `ERR-CHART-PAINTED-NO-MARKS`; widen the slot or use fewer columns. `WARN-TABLE-CRAMPED`: set the board root's `style.frame.width` to the width it suggests (a table has no `frame`).
4. A board with no errors is done: no curl, no reopening a board, no re-running queries, no edits, notes included.{{ cli(' Stop the server unless a link was asked for.') }}

